        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph A. Loftus, George P. Shultz\n- Organizations: The New York Times, International Brotherhood of Teamsters, U.S. Department of Labor, U.S. Department of the Treasury\n- Roles: reporter, communications assistant, economist, statesman, businessman\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph A. Loftus (1907–1990) was a 20th-century American reporter for The New York Times.\n- Joseph A. Loftus covered unions extensively, including the International Brotherhood of Teamsters, while working for The New York Times.\n- Joseph A. Loftus later worked as a communications assistant to George P. Shultz at the U.S. Department of Labor and the U.S. Department of the Treasury.\n- George Pratt Shultz, born on December 13, 1920, is an American economist, statesman, and businessman.",
